data.comment:
EN: Failed QSOs: {0}
    NOTE: Same link once QSOs have failed this run. {0} is a count. Keep it short. Written without brackets on purpose - as "Failed QSOs ({0})" the machine pass moved the bracket and returned "(){0})", which reads as "Failed QSOs ()2)". Punctuation wrapped tightly around a placeholder does not survive translation reliably.
    REVIEW: the machine pass ran a product name into the next word and a space was inserted to separate them. Check that the wording around it reads naturally.

data.value:
Kunde inte öppna {0} Från:

{1}

Använd mapplänken och importera filen till DXKeeper Därifrån.

data.comment:
EN: Could not open {0}:
{1}
Use the folder link and import the file into DXKeeper from there. NOTE: {0} is a filename, {1} is an operating-system error message. Do not translate either. REVIEW: the machine pass ran a product name into the next word and a space was inserted to separate them. Check that the wording around it reads naturally.

EN: Could not open the folder:

{0}
    NOTE: {0} is an operating-system error message - do not translate it.

EN: Nothing has been written to the error log yet:

{0}
    NOTE: {0} is the full path of ErrorLog.txt - do not translate it.

EN: Could not open the help page:

{0}
    NOTE: {0} is an operating-system error message - do not translate it.

EN: Could not listen on UDP port {0}: {1}
    NOTE: Used both as a dialog and as a log line. {0} is a port number, {1} is an operating-system error message.
    REVIEW: the machine pass ran a product name into the next word and a space was inserted to separate them. Check that the wording around it reads naturally.

EN: *** {0}: DXKeeper DELETED the original but did not log the edit{1} - the edited QSO is in {2}, import it. Reason: {3}
    NOTE: The most serious message this program emits: DXKeeper no longer holds the QSO at all. Keep the *** marker. {0} callsign, {1} an optional " (TCP 52001)" tag, {2} a filename, {3} a reason from the Fail* strings.
    REVIEW: the machine pass ran a product name into the next word and a space was inserted to separate them. Check that the wording around it reads naturally.

EN: *** {0}: DXKeeper DELETED the original, the edit was not logged{1}, AND the edit could not be saved to {2}. Reason: {3}
    NOTE: As AlertReplaceLostQso, but the recovery file could not be written either - the QSO is unrecoverable. Keep the *** marker.
    REVIEW: the machine pass ran a product name into the next word and a space was inserted to separate them. Check that the wording around it reads naturally.

EN: DXKeeper did not confirm {0}{1}{2}: {3}
    NOTE: {0} a short description of the QSO, {1} an optional " (TCP 52001)" tag, {2} AlertSavedTo or AlertNotSavedTo or empty, {3} a reason from the Fail* strings.
    REVIEW: the machine pass ran a product name into the next word and a space was inserted to separate them. Check that the wording around it reads naturally.

EN: Version {0}
    NOTE: {0} is a version number such as 2.0.0.
    NOT TRANSLATED: left in English deliberately - either a do-not-translate entry, or the machine pass damaged it and was rejected.

EN: Could not open the licence file:

{0}
    NOTE: {0} is an operating-system error message - do not translate it.

